WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:09.222
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:15.170
Unit sixteen: Weather Forecast. In this unit, you will make predictions about the weather.

4
00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:17.161
Forecast.

5
00:00:17.861 --> 00:00:20.964
Forecast means a report that says what the weather will be like.

6
00:00:21.264 --> 00:00:23.472
Let's check the weather forecast.

7
00:00:24.172 --> 00:00:27.034
Your turn. Say: Forecast.

8
00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:30.735
Forecast.

9
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:32.484
Will.

10
00:00:33.184 --> 00:00:35.555
Will means used to say what we think will happen.

11
00:00:35.855 --> 00:00:37.181
It will rain later.

12
00:00:37.881 --> 00:00:40.464
Your turn. Say: Will.

13
00:00:43.164 --> 00:00:43.968
Will.

14
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:45.915
Degrees.

15
00:00:46.615 --> 00:00:49.485
Degrees means units for measuring temperature.

16
00:00:49.785 --> 00:00:51.436
It's thirty-four degrees today.

17
00:00:52.136 --> 00:00:54.719
Your turn. Say: Degrees.

18
00:00:57.419 --> 00:00:58.397
Degrees.

19
00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:00.373
Thunderstorm.

20
00:01:01.073 --> 00:01:04.733
Thunderstorm means a storm with thunder, lightning and heavy rain.

21
00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:06.788
There will be a thunderstorm tonight.

22
00:01:07.488 --> 00:01:10.199
Your turn. Say: Thunderstorm.

23
00:01:12.899 --> 00:01:13.935
Thunderstorm.

24
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.288
Sunny spells.

25
00:01:16.988 --> 00:01:19.939
Sunny spells means short times when the sun shines.

26
00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:22.158
There will be sunny spells in the morning.

27
00:01:22.858 --> 00:01:25.916
Your turn. Say: Sunny spells.

28
00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:29.850
Sunny spells.

29
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:31.514
Humid.

30
00:01:32.214 --> 00:01:34.353
Humid means hot and wet in the air.

31
00:01:34.653 --> 00:01:36.525
Phnom Penh is very humid.

32
00:01:37.225 --> 00:01:39.541
Your turn. Say: Humid.

33
00:01:42.241 --> 00:01:43.056
Humid.

34
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:44.854
Tomorrow.

35
00:01:45.554 --> 00:01:47.588
Tomorrow means the day after today.

36
00:01:47.888 --> 00:01:49.493
Tomorrow will be cloudy.

37
00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:53.182
Your turn. Say: Tomorrow.

38
00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:56.686
Tomorrow.

39
00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:58.615
Temperature.

40
00:01:59.315 --> 00:02:02.069
Temperature means how hot or cold something is.

41
00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:04.009
The temperature will be high.

42
00:02:04.709 --> 00:02:07.303
Your turn. Say: Temperature.

43
00:02:10.003 --> 00:02:11.004
Temperature.

44
00:02:12.017 --> 00:02:14.005
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:14.305 --> 00:02:16.490
Sreypich, did you see the weather forecast?

46
00:02:17.783 --> 00:02:20.180
Yes. It will be sunny in the morning.

47
00:02:21.483 --> 00:02:22.554
Will it be hot?

48
00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.697
Yes, it will be thirty-four degrees and very humid.

49
00:02:27.983 --> 00:02:29.159
And in the evening?

50
00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.288
There will be a thunderstorm. Take an umbrella!

51
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:37.767
Grammar focus: Will plus verb (predictions).

52
00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:40.487
It will rain tomorrow. It will be hot.

53
00:02:40.787 --> 00:02:46.923
'Will' is the same for everyone: I will, it will, they will. The short form is 'll.

54
00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.383
Now read and listen. Tomorrow's Weather.

55
00:02:50.683 --> 00:02:52.706
Here is tomorrow's weather forecast.

56
00:02:54.017 --> 00:02:57.375
In the morning, there will be sunny spells, and it will be humid.

57
00:02:58.683 --> 00:03:02.900
In the afternoon, the temperature will be thirty-four degrees.

58
00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:07.296
In the evening, there will be a thunderstorm with heavy rain.

59
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:10.153
Don't forget your umbrella!

60
00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.940
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.798
It blank rain tomorrow.

62
00:03:16.098 --> 00:03:19.670
A, will. B, wills. C, is will.

63
00:03:23.683 --> 00:03:25.462
The answer is A: will.

64
00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.286
A storm with thunder and lightning is a blank.

65
00:03:29.586 --> 00:03:33.483
A, thunderstorm. B, sunny spell. C, forecast.

66
00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.727
The answer is A: thunderstorm.

67
00:03:41.217 --> 00:03:43.042
Hot and wet in the air means blank.

68
00:03:43.342 --> 00:03:47.054
A, humid. B, cold. C, dry.

69
00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.841
The answer is A: humid.

70
00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:58.245
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you think the weather will be like tomorrow?

71
00:04:03.545 --> 00:04:08.191
I think it will be hot and sunny in the morning, but there will probably be rain in the afternoon.

72
00:04:08.491 --> 00:04:10.212
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:15.355
Great work today! You learned eight new words and will plus verb (predictions).

74
00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:19.016
Today's value is being prepared. Get ready before you go.

75
00:04:19.316 --> 00:04:22.038
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:22.338 --> 00:04:25.106
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

